cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
title: MMgr
abstract: >-
  Zero-heap memory manager in C11 with a fully deterministic footprint. Confinia,
  pools, spans and rings are carved out of a single borrowed region and reached by
  asserted offset, so every allocation is decided at compile time and there is no
  malloc anywhere. Scanning is SWAR-accelerated, with the word width chosen at the
  ingestion path so the rest of the code is width-agnostic. Every translation unit
  is host-buildable and host-testable.
type: software
